Shared semaphore publication regression
======================================

Run: python3 developer/debug/test/exec/initsemaphoreonce_host.py

The actual InitSemaphoreOnce body executes under ASan/UBSan with sixteen host
clients racing one shared publication word and an Exec gate represented by a
host mutex. All 1,600 successful calls observe a completely initialized object,
with exactly one initializer invocation. Invalid arguments/state and a busy
nonwaiting gate must be refused. A published word bypasses the gate.

This checks publication protocol and control flow; host pthread scheduling is
not AROS scheduling. Rebuild Exec, pthread, headers, consumers and SDK artifacts
coherently, and qualify native first use before claiming runtime acceptance.
The publication word belongs to pthread_types.h, the common C-only public
layout; a new Exec function and private gate require matching Exec imports.
